RunInfo: >
  Requires independent e+p and e+n samples for all four physical
  lepton-target helicities, with POSNLO and NEGNLO generated separately.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [[e+, p+], [e+, n]]
Energies: [[27.6, 0.938272], [27.6, 0.939565]]
Description: >
  Reconstructs fixed-target DIS and hadron kinematics from the highest-energy
  prompt outgoing positron, excluding leptons from hadron decays. It applies
  the main Born-level truth cuts using a circular lepton-angle envelope, not
  the rectangular year-dependent HERMES spectrometer response, and fills normalized
  identified-pion and identified-kaon yields in the one-, two-, and
  three-dimensional HERMES grids. Proton and neutron samples are retained
  separately for the deuteron impulse approximation. Charge-difference
  observables are formed externally from normalized positive- and
  negative-hadron yields; auxiliary histograms retain their same-event
  covariance. The optional azimuthal output is a helicity-summed unpolarized
  yield moment; it is diagnostic-only and is not overlaid on the published
  A_parallel(phi) cosine-fit amplitude.
